  "_doc": [
    "Where the Character Advancement window puts each node of each element's two trees in ring mode (AdvancementLayout.place). Written by tools/ui/advancement_layout.py from data/sway/skill_tree.json, moves.json and data/ui/advancement.json; then hand-tuned by eye in 'pins' (re-running the tool keeps a tuned pin while its id is still in the tree, adds new ids at the algorithm's place and drops gone ones; --reset puts every pin back).",
    "pins.<element>.<left|right>: {node id or root:<move>/<mode> (root:passive/<id> for the passive line): [col, row]} on the diamond lattice (version 2, the tool's lattice(): a col is layout.pitch_x pixels, a row layout.pitch_y; a row's cols are whole on even rows and halves on odd ones, so each pick sits diagonally under the one before it; the gated kinds sit below one gate row). The members of a choice share one place (the first member's is used). The window centres the pinned grid in its zone and spreads its pitch to fill it (layout.min_pitch_* to max_pitch_*, fill_margin kept clear). A hand-tuned pin must keep the lattice's rule (tests/ui/test_advancement.gd checks it).",
    "generated: the band algorithm's own places (the GDScript fallback for an unpinned id and world mode), untouched by hand: tests/ui/test_advancement.gd checks the GDScript algorithm gives the same numbers, and that every ring-visible node has a pin; re-run the tool when the tree changes."
  ],
